1. ANet-Drone4D may be utilized commercially, including as a backend
   service for other applications (for example, by embedding the world
   runtime, the World Package tools or the Web sandbox in your own
   product) and by running it on your own infrastructure. Should the
   conditions below be met, a commercial license must be obtained from the
   producer:

   a. Multi-tenant hosted service: Unless explicitly authorized by the
      producer in writing, you may not use the ANet-Drone4D source code to
      operate a multi-tenant hosted simulation or digital twin service.
      - Hosted simulation or digital twin service definition: a service,
        reached over a network, that runs ANet-Drone4D, or any other
        program built from or derived from ANet-Drone4D source code, to
        build, host, stream or simulate worlds, environments, vehicles,
        sensors or agents; for example a hosted Web sandbox, a hosted
        realtime gateway (`awr.rt.v1`) or REST API, or a service that
        builds World Packages from data its users provide.
      - Multi-tenant hosted service definition: a hosted simulation or
        digital twin service offered, publicly or commercially, to
        multiple unrelated organizations or individuals for their own use,
        such as building or simulating their own worlds, running their own
        scenarios, or connecting their own vehicles or agents. Two parties
        are unrelated when neither controls the other and they are not
        under common control ("control" as defined for "Legal Entity" in
        the Apache License 2.0).
      - The following are not multi-tenant hosted services and need no
        authorization:
        (i)   a service used by one individual, or used only within one
              organization, including the entities that control it, that
              it controls or that are under common control with it, and
              their employees and contractors acting on their behalf;
        (ii)  a research or teaching service: a service operated by or for
              a university, a school, a public research institution or a
              non-profit research organization, and used for research,
              teaching or learning, including by its collaborators,
              students and course participants from other institutions,
              for which no fee or other consideration is charged and which
              is not offered as part of, or to promote, a paid product or
              service;
        (iii) letting others watch an instance that you run for your own
              purposes, for example in a demonstration, a review or an
              exhibition.

   b. LOGO and copyright information: In the process of using
      ANet-Drone4D's user interfaces, you may not remove or modify the
      ANet LOGO or copyright information in them. You may add your own
      name or marks alongside them. This restriction is inapplicable to
      uses of ANet-Drone4D that do not involve these user interfaces, such
      as using its Python packages or World Package tools as a library, or
      running the runtime headless behind your own application.
      - User interface definition: (1) the Web sandbox: the `apps/web/`
        directory of ANet-Drone4D and the pages built from it, including
        the application header, the loading and empty screens, the about
        dialog, the generated reports and the favicon; (2) the command-line
        interface: the output of `awr`, such as its version, help, banner
        and status lines.
      - "LOGO" means the ANet logo and marks as they appear in these user
        interfaces (for example `apps/web/public/brand/anet-logo.svg`, a
        copy of `docs/media/anet-logo.svg` of ANet, and the Agent Network
        Research avatar in `apps/web/public/brand/`); "copyright
        information" means the copyright and attribution notices shown by
        them.

